# SDDRA Work Plan

Purpose:
  Phase-based work plan for SDDRA system development.
  Each phase has clear goals, tasks, and deliverables.
  Track progress by phase and task.

Owns: WORK-PLAN.sdd

## Phase 1: Foundation & Structure (COMPLETED)

Status: Completed

Goals:
  Establish core system structure and immutable rules

Deliverables:
  - .sdd/ system with immutable files
  - Chain graph (D0 with 6 arms)
  - Protocol/ROOT.sdd (universal rules)
  - PROJECT.sdd (root router)
  - INDEX.sdd (routing table)
  - Templates system (.sdd/templates/)
  - Decision ledger engine
  - Task lifecycle engine

Key Decisions:
  - Two-language model (.sdd/ vs project/)
  - Immutability of .sdd/ files
  - Human gates at every stage
  - Token economy and budgets

Files Created: 300+

---

## Phase 2: Skills & Knowledge Base (COMPLETED)

Status: Completed

Goals:
  Build comprehensive engineering skills library

Deliverables:
  - Skills organized by technology (L1-L5)
  - Languages: Go, Rust, Java, Python, C#, C++, TypeScript, JavaScript, Swift, Kotlin, Ruby, PHP
  - Frameworks: React, Flutter, Next.js, NestJS, Spring Boot, Django, FastAPI, Express, etc.
  - Databases: PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Redis, MySQL, Cassandra, Elasticsearch
  - Platforms: Docker, Kubernetes, AWS, GCP, Azure, Terraform
  - Cross-cutting: Testing, Security, Architecture, Observability

Skills Count: 100+ skill files

